{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Scholarship Application Summary",
  "subtitle": "Key metrics and trends for the board",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Applicants",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Approved Applications",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\"='Approved'",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Pending Applications",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\"='Pending'",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Rejected Applications",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\"='Rejected'",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Average Marks by Category",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Category\" AS category, AVG(\"Marks %\") AS avg_marks FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "category",
    "y": [
     "avg_marks"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Monthly Application Trend",
    "sql": "SELECT SUBSTR(\"DOB\",1,7) AS month, COUNT(*) AS total FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "month",
    "y": [
     "total"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top 10 Applicants by Marks",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Sr No\" AS sr_no, \"Naam\" AS name, \"Marks %\" AS marks, \"Status\" AS status FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" ORDER BY 3 DESC LIMIT 10"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The board can see that the total number of scholarship applicants is {{p1.n}}, with {{p2.n}} approved, {{p3.n}} pending, and {{p4.n}} rejected. The bar chart shows that the highest average marks are in the {{p5.category}} category, with an average of {{p5.avg_marks}}%. The line chart indicates a steady increase in applications over the months, peaking in {{p6.month}} with {{p6.total}} submissions. Finally, the table lists the top 10 applicants by marks, highlighting the most promising candidates for further review."
 },
